From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dubzer <me@dubzer.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:28:07 +0300
Subject: Optimize attachment photo and video opening

Prepare photo textures before their first draw, including memory-cache
hits. Animate the thumbnail without a hardware layer or opacity fade for
the whole viewer. Show bottom controls immediately and reuse the stock
selector fade and slide on every opening, including the first.

On Android 14+, preallocate a GPU buffer after the attachment sheet opens,
then capture the chat and gallery on tap. Fade this frozen backdrop to
black during opening so the underlying windows can stop drawing sooner.
Hide only the source thumbnail while recording, retaining the sheet
background and overlapping toolbar. Fall back to an opaque black backdrop
when capture is unavailable.

Clip captions before their temporary alpha layers, draw edge shadows with
direct gradients, and disable viewer blur. Keep stock button backgrounds
and video timeline behavior, respecting the global glass-glare setting.

Controlled by Optimized attachment menu (optimized_attachment_menu), off
by default. Smaller initial photo resolution and high-resolution loading
on zoom or editing remain in the separate attachment-preview-resolution
patch and fast_attachment_previews setting.
